+
+---
+
+## Context — what the ticket said, and what is actually wrong
+
+SCC-456 was raised by SCC-451, which measured four drifted doors in
+`Projects/sudo-command-center` and refused to hide them in a close-out row. That measurement
+reproduces exactly:
+
+| door | master | clone | differing lines |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `smh-quick-dev.md` | 399 | 529 | 690 |
+| `cicd-quick-dev.md` | 483 | 407 | 502 |
+| `smh-non-crit-pr-push.md` | 176 | 168 | 28 |
+| `cicd-non-crit-pr-push.md` | 236 | 208 | 54 |
+
+The ticket's scope — reconcile those four by hand, per hunk, preserving placeholder tokens — is
+the wrong fix, and this plan does not do it. Three measurements say why.
+
+**1. The four are a third of the problem.** Normalising every master through the template's own
+placeholder substitutions and diffing all 66 shared doors gives **44 drifted, 3,689 residual
+lines**. The ticket's four are 1,264 of them.
+
+**2. The repo is generated, not maintained.** `docs/workspace-standard.md:260` states it outright:
+*"the **published teaching edition** of this lobby — a sanitized export, never edited in place"*,
+generated by `export-teaching-edition.ps1`. Hand-editing four door bodies would be overwritten by
+the next export, because nothing flows back.
+
+**3. The generator lives on a branch `main` has never seen.** `origin/claude/teaching-edition` is
+**396 commits behind `origin/main` and 37 ahead**, last touched 2026-09-04 — the same day the
+published repo's last commit landed (*"Refresh command center teaching edition from
+claude/teaching-edition"*). The drift is one fact wearing 44 masks: the export has not run in eight
+days, because the only place it can run from is a branch that stopped absorbing `main`.
+
+### The operator's workflow, and the defect that breaks it
+
+Ruled this session: the published edition exists so team members can read Mr. Hatter's workflow and
+keep it current with `git pull`; they then add their own projects from the `sudo-project-skeleton`
+repo. That model is sound end to end — projects are thin and read their law from the centre they sit
+in, so a team member's project reads from *their* teaching-edition clone and nothing reaches back
+into this workspace.
+
+But the publish step is broken in a way that hits those readers directly. The exporter **refuses a
+non-empty target** (`export-teaching-edition.ps1:244-247`) so that stale files cannot survive a
+refresh invisibly. The consequence is that whoever publishes exports to a fresh folder and copies it
+over the repo — and **a copy adds and overwrites but never removes.**
+
+Measured: the published edition carries **84 files `main` has deleted**, including whole retired
+subsystems.
+
+| what is still in the team's copy | retired by |
+|---|---|
+| the entire `.agents/workflows/` door set (35 files) | SCC-394 — Antigravity's workflow door retired |
+| 15 design skills (`animate`, `apple-design`, `prototype`, …) | SCC-420 — consolidated into `/smh-designer` |
+| the v2 autopilot lane (5 doors) | SCC-430 |
+| `smh-quick-fix.md` + its skill | SCC-445 — the quick lane became `/smh-quick-dev` |
+| `evidence_extract.py` + its test | SCC-447 |
+
+A reader today sees `/smh-quick-fix` in their menu, invokes it, and gets a door no rule, SOP or test
+in the system still matches. That is worse than stale — it is confidently wrong. In the other
+direction the copy is **missing 80 lobby files**, including `/smh-designer`, `epic_mode.py`,
+`scope_check.py`, `inert-paths.json`, `critical-surfaces.json`, three hooks and ~30 tests.
+
+### Why the branch is storage, not a pipeline stage
+
+The branch holds exactly two things: the **engine** (exporter, manifest, `replacements/`, validator,
+its 1,026-line test) and the **tutor** (`/smh-tour`, `/smh-training`, the `training-mode` rule and
+its `.training-mode` sentinel).
+
+The engine can move to `main` today with no consequence, because the manifest already excludes
+`export-teaching-edition.ps1`, `teaching-edition/` and `test_teaching_edition.py` from its own
+export — they were built never to ship. The tutor cannot: it must appear in the export, so today it
+must exist in the source tree, and putting it on `main` would give the lobby two doors nobody there
+uses and force every door-parity test to carry an exception.
+
+So the tutor needs an **overlay**: files the export *adds* from a directory the lobby otherwise
+ignores. The manifest already has the same machinery pointed the other way (`transforms` replaces an
+exported file with one from `replacements/`), so this is one new block, not a new mechanism.
+
+Once both move, the branch has nothing unique left in it, the 396-commit merge disappears
+permanently, and the chain goes from three stages to two.
+
+### What is already true and must not regress
+
+- The exporter's **leak scan cannot be skipped** — it checks every exported byte for `Daniel`,
+  `dlohneiss`, `dlohn`, the machine name, `AviationChat`, `NEXgen`, `Sudo_Hatter_Command` and the
+  real Jira site. This is a **public** repo; that scan is the only thing between the workspace and
+  the internet, and no step in this plan may bypass or weaken it.
+- The published repo's history is **commit-on-top** (7 commits, each a refresh). Team clones depend
+  on that. Nothing here may force-push or re-init it.
